[38;5;252m[1m## Bug found and fixed[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The C is built at [38;5;10m-O0[0m, so every function is compiled literally with no inlining. The translation emulates x86 SSE NaN propagation in software ([38;5;10mmulss[0m/[38;5;10maddss[0m/[38;5;10msubss[0m helpers pinning which operand is the destination), because a binary SSE op returns the [3mdestination[23m operand when both operands are NaN with different payloads. Several sites still used plain Rust [38;5;10m*[0m and [38;5;10m+[0m, and LLVM swaps commutative operands when it inlines — so the wrong NaN payload propagated.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
I disassembled the C and read the actual destination register at every commutative float site, then converted them. Affected: [38;5;10mc2Mulvs[0m, [38;5;10mc2Clip[0m's [38;5;10md0 * d1[0m, [38;5;10mc22[0m/[38;5;10mc23[0m's [38;5;10mdiv[0m sums and [38;5;10mc2Det2(..) * area[0m products, [38;5;10mc2Witness[0m/[38;5;10mc2L[0m's [38;5;10mden * u[0m, [38;5;10mc2GJK[0m's [38;5;10mrA + rB[0m, and the [38;5;10mA.r + B.r[0m / [38;5;10mA.r + depth[0m / [38;5;10mdepths[i] += A.r[0m sites in the manifold functions. First caught by [38;5;10mc2Intersect[0m returning [38;5;10m0xffebcdef[0m where the C returns [38;5;10m0xffc00000[0m.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m## Undefined behaviour in the C, and what it means[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;10mc2MakeProxy[0m has no [38;5;10mC2_TYPE_POLY[0m case, so [38;5;10mc2GJK[0m's [38;5;10mc2Proxy pA/pB[0m (at [38;5;10mrbp-0x100[0m/[38;5;10mrbp-0x150[0m) stay uninitialized for a polygon operand. This is reachable from ordinary input — [38;5;10momni_manifold[0m with an AABB and a capsule goes [38;5;10mc2AABBtoCapsuleManifold[0m → [38;5;10mc2CapsuletoPolyManifold[0m → [38;5;10mc2GJK[0m.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Measured on a fresh (zero-filled) thread stack, the C reads all zeros and agrees with the translation exactly, which is the behaviour the translation models. Because [38;5;10mptr_from_parts[0m never frees, though, the first few calls in a process make glibc set up its arena; [38;5;10msysmalloc[0m/[38;5;10mbrk[0m use far more stack than the steady state and write into that region. Result: [1m1 divergence in 300 000 calls, at call index 2[22m, with the identical input agreeing on every replay. Concurrent allocation can also give [38;5;10mc2Proxy::count[0m a large positive value, making [38;5;10mc2Support[0m walk off the array and crash the C outright.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The tests therefore warm the allocator, zero the callee stack region before each C call, serialize the comparison loops, and build failure messages lazily (allocating inside the loop was itself perturbing [38;5;10mmalloc[0m). [38;5;10mpoly_proxy_reference.rs[0m documents and asserts this, comparing the C on a brand-new thread stack against the Rust. No deterministic implementation can match the C during arena warm-up; that residual is inherent to the C.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
